    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Suicide is a significant public health concern that can have long-term negative consequences for individuals, families, and communities. Over 700,000 people die by suicide every year, and it is the fourth largest cause of mortality among 15-19-year-olds, with low- and middle-income (LMIC) nations accounting for 77% of worldwide suicides.",
